  "family": "Myrtaceae",
  "memo": "This tree features a striking, rough bark that ranges in color from dark brown to black, providing a dramatic contrast to its slender, blue-green leaves. It produces clusters of small, cream-colored to pink flowers that attract bees and birds, adding a lively touch to urban landscapes. Its branches have a graceful, slightly drooping habit, creating a soft, cascading effect. This tree is well-suited for dry climates, thriving in full sun and requiring minimal water once established. Its resilience and unique appearance make it a popular choice for parks and large gardens.",
